module gunbc.recurring_failure_mode.unresolved_signature_skips_call_shape_judgment

import std.types { NonEmptyStr }
import gunbc.recurring_failure_mode { BelowCeiling, FoundBelowTheLadder, RecurringFailureMode, RungRead }
import gunbc.guarantee_rung { MechanicallyPreventable }
import gunbc.rung_climb { ClimbableButUnbuilt }

data unresolved_signature_skips_call_shape_judgment: RecurringFailureMode = RecurringFailureMode {
  identity: "unresolved_signature_skips_call_shape_judgment" as NonEmptyStr,

  rung: RungRead { found_at: FoundBelowTheLadder, standing: BelowCeiling { current: FoundBelowTheLadder, ceiling: MechanicallyPreventable, blocker: ClimbableButUnbuilt, trigger_capability: "the capability of resolving a signature for a bare callee spelling that matches a kernel method template name without an import or a local declaration (func_env_declared_func_sig or parent_closure_callable_candidates answering the unimported spelling), so the direct-call shape wall sees sig Present and fires uniformly; measured at run time by test.claim.sig_unresolved_fallthrough_witness census leg, which counts the sites where it does not." } },

  receipts: [
    "**a call whose callee resolves NO signature bypasses every call-shape judgment, because the shape wall is gated on the signature being PRESENT -- the absence is not a judgment result, it is the absence of a judgment. The direct-call shape wall (direct_call_shape_wall_note) validates argument labels only in the branch where the callee's signature resolved (sig Present); on sig Absent the call falls through to the method bridge, which binds arguments positionally and never compares labels to any declared parameter list. The invalid state: the SAME mislabeled call -- a labeled argument naming a parameter the callee does not declare -- is REFUSED when the callee is locally declared (func_env puts the sig in scope, sig Present, the wall fires with CallArgumentNameUnknown) and ACCEPTED SILENTLY when the same callee name is unimported and undeclared and so resolves no signature. Wrongness is thereby gated on the RESOLVER's coverage rather than on the program, which is the sibling absorption this row shares with `gunbc.recurring_failure_mode.unresolved_callee_conflated_with_dispatched_elsewhere` seen from the call-shape side: that row owns the miss being absorbed downstream after the dispatch paths answered; this row owns the call-shape judgment being SKIPPED because the signature never arrived.**",

    "**MEASURED, NOT INFERRED. The asymmetry is executed by two controls in `dag/test/claim/sig_unresolved_fallthrough_witness.dag`: `locally_declared_kernel_name_mislabeled_call_is_refused` (a mislabeled call to a locally-declared kernel method template name refuses with CallArgumentNameUnknown -- the compiler IS capable at the shape layer) and `locally_declared_correctly_labeled_call_compiles_clean` (the wall does not over-refuse). The blind spot itself is NOT enrolled as a passing assertion: a leg that greened while a mislabeled unimported call compiled clean would be the bug enrolled as an asset, green only while the compiler stays wrong (gunbc.design_argument::fail_closed: silent wrongness is below the ladder and forbidden outright). The blind spot is carried HERE, as this row. Its population is computed AT RUN TIME by the census leg of the same witness -- names drawn from the algebra authority (`std.algebra` `all_algebra_template_names`, the same `AlgebraFieldTemplate` rows `algebra_method_template_name` consults), the predicate and filters in `.dag`, printed from the claim with the predicate, the module count scanned, the head sha and the binary sha256. NO COMMITTED PROJECTION OF THE MEASUREMENT IS FILED (gunbc.design_argument::how_to_work: a census without a concrete retained consumer is retired; a hand shell implementing semantics expressible in `.dag` is presumed scaffold): the consumer is this row's trigger and the roadmap node `call-signature-resolution-coverage` red_control, and the instrument is the witness itself.**",

    "**DISSOLUTION OF THIS ROW (bounded): the unimported mislabeled call to a kernel method template name REFUSES with a located call-shape cause (CallArgumentNameUnknown or its typed peer naming the callee and the declared parameter list), the census leg's count falls monotonically as resolution coverage lands, and the residual population reaches only sites whose callees are answered by a legitimate dispatch path (pipeline/collection methods, constructors) rather than by no path at all. Closing it is NOT this row's work: the resolution mechanism is the namespace lane (roadmap node `call-signature-resolution-coverage`, boundary `out_of_scope: the resolution mechanism itself`); this row owns the call-shape consequence, and the refusal that belongs at the direct-call tail when no path answers already exists at the ExprCall tail (see the sibling row's refutation of the `can never refuse` wording).**",
  ],

  evidence: [],
}
